hub.com L202: ### Clone this wiki locally\nL203: \nL204: ## Footer\nL205: \nL206: cite79†  © 2026 GitHub, Inc.\nL207: \nL208: ### Footer navigation\nL209: \nL210:   * cite80†Terms†docs.github.com L211:   * cite81†Privacy†docs.github.com L212:   * cite82†Security L213:   * cite83†Status†www.githubstatus.com L214:   * cite84†Community†github.community L215:   * cite85†Docs†docs.github.com L216:   * cite86†Contact†support.github.com L217:   * Manage cookies\nL218:   * Do not share my personal information\nL219: \nL220:   You can’t perform that action at this time.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nxxHash: xxHash (https://xxhash.com/doc/v0.8.4/index.html)\nciteturn121view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 5 days ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"turn120view1\",\"lineno\":35}); Total lines: 297\nL13:   1. cite0†XXH32 family L14:      * Classic 32-bit hash function. Simple, compact, and runs on almost all 32-bit and 64-bit systems.\nL15:   2. cite1†XXH64 family L16:      * Classic 64-bit adaptation of XXH32. Just as simple, and runs well on most 64-bit systems (but not 32-bit systems).\nL17:   3. cite2†XXH3 family L18:      * Modern 64-bit and 128-bit hash function family which features improved strength and performance across the board, especially on smaller data. It benefits greatly from SIMD and 64-bit without requiring it.\nL19: ## Benchmarks\nL20: \nL21: The reference system uses an Intel i7-9700K CPU, and runs Ubuntu x64 20.04. The open source benchmark program is compiled with clang v10.0 using -O3 flag.\nL22: Hash Name  | ISA ext  | Width  | Large Data Speed  | Small Data Velocity\nL23: --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nL24: cite3†XXH3_64bits() | AVX2  | 64  | 59.4 GB/s  | 133.1\nL25: MeowHash  | AES-NI  | 128  | 58.2 GB/s  | 52.5\nL26: cite4†XXH3_128bits() | AVX2  | 128  | 57.9 GB/s  | 118.1\nL27: CLHash  | PCLMUL  | 64  | 37.1 GB/s  | 58.1\nL28: cite3†XXH3_64bits() | SSE2  | 64  | 31.5 GB/s  | 133.1\nL29: cite4†XXH3_128bits() | SSE2  | 128  | 29.6 GB/s  | 118.1\nL30: RAM sequential read  |  | N/A  | 28.0 GB/s  | N/A\nL31: ahash  | AES-NI  | 64  | 22.5 GB/s  | 107.2\nL32: City64  |  | 64  | 22.0 GB/s  | 76.6\nL33: T1ha2  |  | 64  | 22.0 GB/s  | 99.0\nL34: City128  |  | 128  | 21.7 GB/s  | 57.7\nL35: FarmHash  | AES-NI  | 64  | 21.3 GB/s  | 71.9\nL36: cite5†XXH64() |  | 64  | 19.4 GB/s  | 71.0\nL37: SpookyHash  |  | 64  | 19.3 GB/s  | 53.2\nL38: Mum  |  | 64  | 18.0 GB/s  | 67.0\nL39: CRC32C  | SSE4.2  | 32  | 13.0 GB/s  | 57.9\nL40: cite6†XXH32() |  | 32  | 9.7 GB/s  | 71.9\nL41: City32  |  | 32  | 9.1 GB/s  | 66.0\nL42: Blake3*  | AVX2  | 256  | 4.4 GB/s  | 8.1\nL43: Murmur3  |  | 32  | 3.9 GB/s  | 56.1\nL44: SipHash*  |  | 64  | 3.0 GB/s  | 43.2\nL45: Blake3*  | SSE2  | 256  | 2.4 GB/s  | 8.1\nL46: HighwayHash  |  | 64  | 1.4 GB/s  | 6.0\nL47: FNV64  |  | 64  | 1.2 GB/s  | 62.7\nL48: Blake2*  |  | 256  | 1.1 GB/s  | 5.1\nL49: SHA1*  |  | 160  | 0.8 GB/s  | 5.6\nL50: MD5*  |  | 128  | 0.6 GB/s  | 7.8\nL51: Note\nL52: \nL53: \nL54:   * Hashes which require a specific ISA extension are noted. SSE2 is also noted, even though it is mandatory on x64.\nL55:   * Hashes with an asterisk are cryptographic. Note that MD5 is non-cryptographic by modern standards.\nL56:   * Small data velocity is a rough average of algorithm's efficiency for small data. For more accurate information, see the wiki.\nL57:   * More benchmarks and strength tests are found on the wiki: cite7†https://github.com/Cyan4973/xxHash/wiki†github.com L58: ## Usage\nL59: \nL60: All xxHash variants use a similar API. Changing the algorithm is a trivial substitution.\nL61: \nL62: Precondition\nL63:     For functions which take an input and length parameter, the following requirements are assumed:\nL64: \nL65:   * The range from [`input`, `input + length`) is valid, readable memory.\nL66:     * The only exception is if the `length` is `0`, `input` may be `NULL`.\nL67:   * For C++, the objects must have the TriviallyCopyable property, as the functions access bytes directly as if it was an array of `unsigned char`.\nL68: Single Shot\nL69: \nL70: These functions are stateless functions which hash a contiguous block of memory, immediately returning the result. They are the easiest and usually the fastest option.\nL71: \nL72: cite6†XXH32() , cite5†XXH64() , cite3†XXH3_64bits() , cite4†XXH3_128bits() L73: #include <string.h>\nL74: #include \"cite8†xxhash.h \"\nL75: \nL76: // Example for a function which hashes a null terminated string with XXH32().\nL77: \nL78: cite9†XXH32_hash_t hash_string(const char* string, cite9†XXH32_hash_t seed)\nL79: \nL80: {\nL81: \nL82: // NULL pointers are only valid if the length is zero\nL83: \nL84: size_t length = (string == NULL) ? 0 : strlen(string);\nL85: \nL86: return cite6†XXH32 (string, length, seed);\nL87: \nL88: }\nL89: \nL90: cite6†XXH32 L91: \nL92: XXH32_hash_t XXH32(const void *input, size_t length, XXH32_hash_t seed)\nL93: \nL94: Calculates the 32-bit hash of input using xxHash32.\nL95: \nL96: Definition xxhash.h:3207\nL97: cite9†XXH32_hash_t L98: \nL99: uint32_t XXH32_hash_t\nL100: \nL101: An unsigned 32-bit integer.\nL102: \nL103: Definition xxhash.h:588\nL104: \nL105: cite8†xxhash.h L106: \nL107: Streaming\nL108: \nL109: These groups of functions allow incremental hashing of unknown size, even more than what would fit in a size_t.\nL110: \nL111: cite10†XXH32_reset() , cite11†XXH64_reset() , cite12†XXH3_64bits_reset() , cite13†XXH3_128bits_reset() L112: #include <stdio.h>\nL113: \nL114: #include <assert.h>\nL115: #include \"cite8†xxhash.h \"\nL116: \nL117: // Example for a function which hashes a FILE incrementally with XXH3_64bits().\nL118: \nL119: cite14†XXH64_hash_t hashFile(FILE* f)\nL120: \nL121: {\nL122: \nL123: // Allocate a state struct. Do not just use malloc() or new.\nL124: \nL125: cite15†XXH3_state_t * state = cite16†XXH3_createState ();\nL126: \nL127: assert(state != NULL && \"Out of memory!\");\nL128: \nL129: // Reset the state to start a new hashing session.\nL130: \nL131: cite12†XXH3_64bits_reset (state);\nL132: \nL133: char buffer[4096];\nL134: \nL135: size_t count;\nL136: \nL137: // Read the file in chunks\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n〖Unity〗Unity公式のハッシュアルゴリズムxxHash3がCollectionsパッケージに入っているので使ってみる - はなちるのマイノート (https://www.hanachiru-blog.com/entry/2023/09/07/120000)\nciteturn121view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"turn120view3\",\"lineno\":85}); Total lines: 402\nL55: > // DeepL翻訳\nL56: > xxHash は非常に高速なハッシュアルゴリズムで、RAM 速度の限界で処理します。コードの移植性が高く、すべてのプラットフォーム（リトル/ビッグエンディアン）で同一のハッシュを生成します。ライブラリには以下のアルゴリズムが含まれています：\nL57: >\nL58: >   * XXH32 : 32 ビット演算を使用して 32 ビットハッシュを生成します。\nL59: >   * XXH64 : 64 ビット演算を使用して 64 ビットハッシュを生成する。\nL60: >   * XXH3 (v0.8.0以降): ベクトル化された算術を用いて64ビットまたは128ビットのハッシュを生成する。128ビットハッシュはXXH128と呼ばれる。\nL61: >\nL63: cite13†GitHub - Cyan4973/xxHash: Extremely fast non-cryptographic hash algorithm†github.com L64: 公式の`Collections`パッケージの中に`xxHash3`の実装が`public`で公開されています。\nL65: cite14†Class xxHash3 | Collections | 2.2.0†hatenablog-parts.com cite15†docs.unity3d.com†docs.unity3d.com L66: \nL67:     public static uint2 Hash64(void *input, long length)\nL68:     public static uint2 Hash64(void *input, long length, ulong seed)\nL69:     public static uint2 Hash64<T>(in T input) where T : struct\nL70: \nL71: \nL72:     public static uint4 Hash128(void *input, long length)\nL73:     public static uint4 Hash128(void *input, long length, ulong seed)\nL74:     public static uint4 Hash128(void *input, void *destination, long length)\nL75:     public static uint4 Hash128(void *input, void *destination, long length, ulong seed)\nL76:     public static uint4 Hash128<T>(in T input) where T : struct\nL77: また`xxHash3`の中身は`Burst`により最適化されており、返り値も`Mathematics`の`uint4`が利用されています。ここからも`SIMD`を活用した最適化がなされていそうな雰囲気が伺えます。\nL78: ### インストール方法\nL79: \nL80: `PackageManager`より`Collections`パッケージがインストールされているか確認してください。されていない場合はインストールします。\nL81: \nL82: cite16†Image†cdn-ak.f.st-hatena.com Collectionsパッケージ\nL83: \nL84: ### 使い方\nL85: #### NativeArray利用例\nL86: \nL87:     public void Start()\nL88:     {\nL89:         // unmanagedなHeap確保\nL90:         NativeArray<byte> input = new NativeArray<byte>(10000, Allocator.Temp, NativeArrayOptions.UninitializedMemory);\nL91:         for (var i = 0; i < input.Length; i++)\nL92:         {\nL93:             input[i] = (byte)(i % 255);\nL94:         }\nL95: \nL96:         unsafe\nL97:         {\nL98:             // Hash値計算\nL99:             uint4 hash128 = xxHash3.Hash128(input.GetUnsafePtr(), input.Length);\nL100:             // uint4(218708217, 638813917, 1325193794, 1873747569)\nL101:             Debug.Log(hash128);\nL102: \nL103:             // Hash値計算\nL104:             var hash64 = xxHash3.Hash64(input.GetUnsafePtr(), input.Length);\nL105: \nL106:             // uint2(218708217, 638813917)\nL107:             Debug.Log(hash64);\nL108:         }\nL109: \nL110:         // NativeArray破棄\nL111:         input.Dispose();\nL112:     }\nL113: #### ManagedHeapの例\nL114: \nL115:     public void Start()\nL116:     {\nL117:         var input = Enumerable.Range(0, 100000).Select(x => (byte)x).ToArray();\nL118: \nL119:         unsafe\nL120:         {\nL121:             fixed (byte* p = input)\nL122:             {\nL123:                 // Hash値計算\nL124:                 uint4 hash128 = xxHash3.Hash128(p, input.Length);\nL125: \nL126:                 // uint4(1566616920, 969907459, 2787069300, 125799814)\nL127:                 Debug.Log(hash128);\nL128: \nL129:                 // Hash値計算\nL130:                 var hash64 = xxHash3.Hash64(p, input.Length);\nL131: \nL132:                 // uint2(1566616920, 969907459)\nL133:                 Debug.Log(hash64);\nL134:             }\nL135:         }\nL136:     }\nL137: ### さいごに\nL138: \nL139: `xxHash3.StreamingState`という複数のデータからハッシュ計算をしてくれる構造体があるので、また別の記事で紹介しようと思ってます。\nL140: cite17†Struct xxHash3.StreamingState | Collections | 2.2.0†hatenablog-parts.com cite18†docs.unity3d.com†docs.unity3d.com L141: \nL142: 制作中ゲーム(ウィッシュリストに追加してくださると開発速度UP)\nL143: \nL144: cite19†iframe†store.steampowered.com L145: \nL146: hanaaaaaachiru cite2†2023-09-07 12:00 L147: \nL148: cite20†iframe†blog.hatena.ne.jp L149: \nL150: スポンサーリンク\nL151: \nL152: コメントを書く\nL153: \nL154:   * もっと読む\nL155: \nL156: cite21†« 〖C#〗Marshal.AllocHGlobal・NativeMemor… cite22†〖C#〗RuntimeHelpers.IsReferenceOrConta… » L157: \nL158: プロフィール\nL159: cite23†id:hanaaaaaachiru cite24†はてなブログPro†blog.hatena.ne.jp L160: \nL161: Unityメインな技術ブログ。\"マイノート\"は\"マイペースなノート\"の略で、名前の通り自由にやっていこうと思います。\nL162: \nL163: cite25†@hanaaaaaachiruをフォロー†x.com L164: \nL165: cite23†このブログについて L166: \nL167: cite26†最新記事 L168: \nL169:   * cite27†〖.NET〗Nullable<T>のTの型が欲しい場合はGetGenericArguments()ではなくGetNullableUnderlyingType()を使おう L170: \nL171: cite3†C# cite28†.NET L172: \nL173:   * cite29†〖.NET〗dotnet/runtimeをmacOSでローカルビルドしてパフォーマンス計測するまでのやり方 L174: \nL175: cite28†.NET L176: \nL177:   * cite30†〖Unity〗Unity Cliのset_autotickのドメインリロード問題がv0.5.0-exp.1にて対応された話 L178: \nL179: cite4†Unity L180:   * cite31†〖Unity〗Unity6.8でCoreCLR GCが導入されてもIL2CPPではBoehm GCなのでGC.Collectの呼び出し方は注意した方が良い話 L181: \nL182: cite4†Unity L183: \nL184:   * cite32†〖C#, Unity〗JetBrains.Annotationsの[MustDisposeResource]はUniTaskにも対応してた話 L185: \nL186: cite4†Unity cite3†C# L187: \nL188: セールアセット\nL189: \nL190: 人気アセット\nL191: \nL192: cite33†iframe†assetstore.unity.com L193: \nL194: 注目記事\nL195: \nL196: セールアセット\nL197: \nL198: cite26†月別アーカイブ L199: \nL200:   * ▼ ▶\nL201: \nL202: cite34†2026 L203:     * cite35†2026 / 9 L204:     * cite36†2026 / 8 L205:     * cite37†2026 / 7 L206:     * cite38†2026 / 6 L207:     * cite39†2026 / 5 L208:     * cite40†2026 / 4 L209:     * cite41†2026 / 3